@inherits RazorBlade.HtmlTemplate
@*
  The widget's shared stylesheet, written once and included by every page.

  A partial rather than a helper: it is an ordinary RazorBlade template, so it composes the way any
  other view does and a page that wants more adds its own <style> after it. There is nothing to
  close and nothing to remember beyond the one line that includes it.

  Selectors are prefixed because a widget's CSS is global to the dashboard page. Whether the console
  isolates each widget is unverified - AWS's own samples write bare `td { }`, which only works if it
  does - so this assumes it does not. See day-one check 3.
*@
<style>
  .ls-meta { color: #687078; font-size: 12px; margin: 4px 0; }
  .ls-empty { color: #687078; font-style: italic; }
</style>
